    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral upper respiratory infection (J06.9)</content>. A cold, with no fever and no sign of pneumonia. Rapid influenza and COVID-19 tests are negative. The white cell count is 2.9 and the neutrophil count 1.3, the expected low point a week after carboplatin and paclitaxel; without a fever this needs no antibiotic and no admission, but a temperature of 38.0 °C or higher would be an emergency (possible febrile neutropenia). Dr. Varghese&apos;s team was told and agrees. [S]<list><item>Fluids, rest, saline nasal spray, and throat lozenges; acetaminophen only after checking her temperature first, so that it does not hide a fever.</item><item>Check her temperature twice a day; call the oncology line at once, day or night, or go to the emergency department for 38.0 °C or more, chills, breathlessness, or feeling unwell.</item><item>Hand washing and a mask in crowds until the counts recover.</item><item>Cycle 3 as planned if the neutrophil count is 1.5 or more on the day.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">High-grade serous ovarian cancer, stage IIIC, on chemotherapy (C56.3)</content>. Second cycle given a week ago on schedule; nausea controlled with ondansetron; no tingling in the hands or feet so far. [S]<list><item>Continue the planned chemotherapy.</item><item>Next review at cycle 4.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Ovarian Cancer/Fallopian Tube Cancer/Primary Peritoneal Cancer, Version 4.2026 (2026); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Prevention and Treatment of Cancer-Related Infections (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Phone check in two days. Call at once for a temperature of 38.0 °C or more. Cycle 3 as booked. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-14: midpoint of chemotherapy: CA-125, blood counts, neuropathy, and menopausal symptoms. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
